  "scenario": "Run a fixed-size Qt Quick Vulkan window in Plasma Wayland. Keep the 10000 microsecond DRM setting and the installed PowerVR ICD. In two sessions, instrument the scheduling decisions and then the render time samples. Match the primary frame to the page flip event and read the active CRTC framebuffer at consecutive vblanks.",
  "expected": "Display a new framebuffer on each refresh and identify where long intervals occur.",
  "observed": "The CRTC changed framebuffer about 30 times per second in both samples. KWin selected a two-period render budget. In long intervals an earlier frame with an eligible target often failed the buffer readiness check and was later dropped.",
