  "limits": [
    "Qt frameSwapped measures the client. The CRTC sample covers the full output. Neither measurement observes light from the panel.",
    "Each scene took 60 seconds. Each CRTC trace contains 360 samples within its scene. Matched intervals use both an observed framebuffer change and a page flip event.",
    "The CPU render query measures elapsed time on the steady clock. Thread CPU accounting excludes time the compositor thread spent off CPU. These traces do not measure GPU execution time.",
    "The stricter dropped-frame join requires a single queued candidate, its own eligible target, a matching worker readiness check and two consecutive field timestamps 16 to 17 ms apart. It excludes two intervals in each trace.",
    "A failed buffer readiness check does not give the time a particular producer fence became ready. Both runs retained the installed scheduling policy."
